# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Corpus data and derived artifacts are NOT tracked.
#
# The CEJC corpus is distributed under a data use agreement and cannot be
# redistributed here. Everything derived from it (utterance tables, monologues,
# feature matrices, model scores) stays local. Identity of the derived files is
# pinned by sha256 instead — see docs/data-availability.md.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
artifacts/**
!artifacts/README.md
!artifacts/.gitkeep

# Exception: the synthetic dataset. It is built from published summary statistics only
# (the descriptive-statistics and correlation tables in reports/, plus record counts
# stated in the manuscript), so it is not derived data under the CEJC agreement and can
# be archived. It is tracked so that a download of this repository can run the pipeline
# without the corpus. Regenerate with `make synthetic`.
!artifacts/synthetic/
!artifacts/synthetic/PROVENANCE.json
!artifacts/synthetic/synthetic_features.parquet
!artifacts/synthetic/synthetic_speaker_metadata.tsv
!artifacts/synthetic/datasets/
!artifacts/synthetic/datasets/*.parquet

data/**
!data/README.md

# Aggregated result tables are reproducible from the scripts; only the figures
# and LaTeX tables that appear in the manuscript are tracked (reports/).

# --- python ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
.hypothesis/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# --- editors / OS ---
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/

# --- LaTeX build products ---
*.aux
*.dvi
*.log
*.out
*.toc
*.bbl
*.blg
*.synctex.gz

# --- scratch ---
tmp/
logs/
*.bak
*.bak.*
*.bak_*
